# Known gaps against ito, kept visible on purpose: `<crate> <reason>`. Each line is a migration still to do, not a decision to stay.
ito-help tsumugi's help.rs lays groups out in 1-4 columns and shrinks to fit without scrolling, which ito-help (one scrolled column over ito_keymap::HelpLine) cannot do; requested as uchmk/ito#10
ito-testcheck tsumugi's examples/make-keycheck still writes TESTING-KEYS.md itself (its own format and ticks); the TESTING-CHECKS.md side already uses ito-testcheck
postcard tsumugi-mux state.rs saves and restores its versioned state file with postcard directly (persistence, not a wire protocol; frame.rs already uses ito_ipc::frame). Share it via ito only if another app needs a versioned binary state file
